From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000014 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Guard Hero <build@guardhero.app>
Date: Mon, 01 Jan 2025 00:00:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] eagleeye: wire URLRequestRedirectJob for tracking param stripping

Completes the MODIFY path in EagleEyeInterceptor. When the EagleEye
URL analyzer strips tracking parameters (utm_*, fbclid, gclid, etc.)
from an allowed request, we previously fell through to ALLOW and lost
the cleaned URL. This patch:

  1. Passes url.spec() (full URL) instead of url.host() in RequestContext
     so that the UrlAnalyzer has the query string to work with.

  2. Returns a URLRequestRedirectJob (307 Temporary Redirect) pointing at
     the cleaned URL instead of nullptr.

  3. Adds three safety checks before issuing the redirect:
       - cleaned URL is well-formed (GURL::is_valid())
       - host must match the original (prevent open redirect)
       - scheme must match the original

  4. Documents the redirect mechanism in detail (same-origin 307, internal
     redirect, CORS behavior, POST-method preservation vs. 301).

Why 307 and not a URL mutation:
  URLRequestInterceptor has no direct API to rewrite the URL in-place.
  The standard approach (used by Brave, uBlock via extension WebRequest API)
  is to issue an internal redirect. The 307 redirect is processed entirely
  within the browser process — the renderer sees a single response at the
  cleaned URL and is never aware of the dirty URL.

Performance:
  The redirect adds ~0 network latency (it is synthetic, not a real HTTP
  response). The only overhead is one extra call to MaybeInterceptRequest()
  on the redirected URL, which is a fast ALLOW (no tracking params).

Chromium files touched:
  chrome/browser/guardhero/eagleeye_interceptor.cc
---
 chrome/browser/guardhero/eagleeye_interceptor.cc | 65 ++++++++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 58 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/chrome/browser/guardhero/eagleeye_interceptor.cc b/chrome/browser/guardhero/eagleeye_interceptor.cc
index aabbcc11..ddeeef22 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/guardhero/eagleeye_interceptor.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/guardhero/eagleeye_interceptor.cc
@@ -27,6 +27,7 @@
+#include "net/url_request/url_request_redirect_job.h"

@@ -120,10 +121,25 @@ net::URLRequestJob* EagleEyeInterceptor::MaybeInterceptRequest(
-  // Pass GURL::host() as context.url (fast path, hostname only).
-  context.url = url.host();
+  // Pass url.spec() (full URL) so the UrlAnalyzer can find and strip
+  // query parameters. ExtractHost() parses the hostname from the spec.
+  context.url = url.spec();

@@ -145,13 +161,52 @@ net::URLRequestJob* EagleEyeInterceptor::MaybeInterceptRequest(
     case eagleeye::Decision::MODIFY: {
-      // TODO(v1.0): return URLRequestRedirectJob
-      return nullptr;
+      const GURL clean_url(result.modified_url);
+
+      // Validate before redirecting — defense against UrlAnalyzer bugs.
+      if (!clean_url.is_valid()) {
+        LOG(WARNING) << "Guard Hero EagleEye: MODIFY produced invalid URL";
+        return nullptr;
+      }
+      if (clean_url.host() != url.host() || clean_url.scheme() != url.scheme()) {
+        LOG(WARNING) << "Guard Hero EagleEye: MODIFY changed host/scheme — refusing";
+        return nullptr;
+      }
+
+      return new net::URLRequestRedirectJob(
+          request, network_delegate, clean_url,
+          net::URLRequestRedirectJob::REDIRECT_307_TEMPORARY_REDIRECT,
+          "EagleEye-TrackingParamStrip");
     }
